--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/reference/issue-leases.md
@@ -0,0 +1,46 @@
+# Issue execution leases
+
+Owner/Assignee records long-term responsibility. An issue execution/write lease
+records one current execution tenure. `kata claim` still assigns an owner; it is
+not an execution lease operation.
+
+Lease authority is local for standalone projects and enabled federation hubs.
+Enabled spokes forward to their hub and only cache its response. Disabled
+bindings do not grant authority. A lease operation only opportunistically
+expires claims in its target project; the background sweeper handles active
+standalone/hub projects and never sweeps spoke caches locally.
+
+The existing HTTP lease routes work for standalone and federation projects:
+
+```text
+GET  /api/v1/projects/{project_id}/issues/{ref}/lease
+POST /api/v1/projects/{project_id}/issues/{ref}/lease/actions/acquire
+POST /api/v1/projects/{project_id}/issues/{ref}/lease/actions/renew
+POST /api/v1/projects/{project_id}/issues/{ref}/lease/actions/release
+POST /api/v1/projects/{project_id}/issues/{ref}/lease/actions/force_release
+```
+
+Use timed leases for agents. Renew automatically well before TTL; graceful
+release is best-effort, while process failure is recovered by expiry. A repeated
+acquire by the same exact principal returns the same ClaimUID, without renewing
+it. A different tenure needs a new execution identity. Retry an uncertain
+acquire with its original attempt identity, not a new HTTP-request identity.
+
+`lease` and `lease_hub_now` remain the shared show fields (the timestamp is local
+for standalone projects). No second standalone lease wire model exists. The
+legacy CLI namespace `kata federation lease` is retained; it does not imply
+that standalone API clients need a federation binding. Force-release remains
+an administrator/host-policy operation and is refused locally on spokes.
+
+Ordinary standalone mutation policy is unchanged: possession of a lease does
+not globally lock comments, links, owner assignment, or other legacy mutations.
+Embedding hosts must enforce worker capabilities server-side. Comments remain
+a shared contribution channel, not an execution-holder privilege.
+
+For strict worker close use [close-v2](http-api.md#exact-execution-lease-close):
+exact ClaimUID and principal validation, issue close, and lease release happen
+in one transaction. Retry with the same Idempotency-Key to recover a receipt
+after release. No lease, expired lease, wrong tenure, wrong holder, or a spoke
+cache cannot authorize strict close. Legacy closes remain available according
+to host policy; they release a live authoritative lease without broadening
+federation violation auditing to standalone projects.
